    "tropical_day": {
      "exposure_ev100": 1.0,
      "fog": {"density": 0.03, "height_falloff": 0.2, "color": "#8FD3F0", "start_distance": 3000, "max_opacity": 1.0, "sky_ambient": 0.0},
      "sky": {"luminance_factor": [2.35, 2.75, 3.1]},
      "sky_light": {"intensity": 0.35},
      "notes": [
        "Rebuild b974f4d tuning: sky x1.3 (zenith #528CBE -> ~#6FA0C8), sky light 0.45->0.35 to keep shadow fill; cave fills #B8D8E6 (neutral), +50% intensity, radius 750/550/750 so the mouth outer walls (#020A14) and crawl walls (#15465C) reach #2E3A40-#3E4A4F. Designer S1 + ART_STYLE: fixed exposure, palette hex = on-screen target. EV100 1.0 = exposure scale 0.5: the 10 lux sun (x0.84 atmosphere, 50 deg) plus sky fill puts sunlit horizontal surfaces at ~1.05x their albedo before the filmic tonemapper (which keeps mid tones, compresses highlights). Tune in steps of 0.25: +0.25 = darker.",
        "Fog: density 0.03 from 30 m (was 0.006 from 40 m). levels.layout.fog_transmittance: Gull Key at 210 m 22% fog (readable), sea edge 400 m 41%, sky 6 deg up 60%, 10 deg 42%, 20 deg 22%, Beacon from spawn 4%. Color = on-screen target (builder undoes exposure + tonemapper); sky_ambient 0 keeps the SkyAtmosphere from adding to it.",
        "Sky: luminance x1.8/2.1/2.4 lifts the steel-blue zenith (~#3E607C in the T-005 PIE shot) toward #8FD3F0 (estimate ~#6095B9); the real-time sky light captures that too, so its intensity 0.45 keeps the shadow fill about where it was. First guesses: check the zenith in the rebuild screenshot."
      ]
    },
    "tropical_dusk": {"exposure_ev100": 0.0, "fog": {"density": 0.012, "height_falloff": 0.2, "color": "#FF9A5A", "start_distance": 2500, "sky_ambient": 0.0}, "notes": "Proposal for T-013 (not built): the sun preset and the EV get tuned together there."},
    "tropical_night": {"exposure_ev100": -3.0, "fog": {"density": 0.02, "height_falloff": 0.15, "color": "#1B2440", "start_distance": 1500, "sky_ambient": 0.0}, "notes": "Proposal for T-013 (not built): night stays dark (fixed EV, no auto brightening), lamps and the Beacon carry it."}
  },
